### 2. What's Deductible?
Even if you take the standard deduction, you can still claim "above-the-line" deductions and business expenses:
*   **Student Loan Interest:** You can deduct up to **$2,500** of the $4,250 you paid. This is an adjustment to income, meaning you get this deduction *in addition* to the standard deduction. (Your combined income of roughly $100k is well below the phase-out limit for married couples).
